# Lead delivery.
# When RESEND_API_KEY is set, the seller lead form sends each submission by
# email (see app/actions/referral.ts). Without it, the form validates and shows
# success but does NOT send or persist anything. Copy this file to `.env.local`
# and fill in the key to go live. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# Note: the to/from addresses are currently HARDCODED in app/actions/referral.ts
#   to:   jamie.nisbet@outlook.be
#   from: Jamie Nisbet Consultancy <noreply@mail.jamienisbet.com>
# We can move them back into env vars later.
#
# Get a key at https://resend.com → API Keys
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The template ID isn't set here — it's not a secret, so it's checked into
# packages/ui/emails/template-ids.ts instead (one file shared by every site,
# rather than one env var per site per template). Publish
# packages/ui/emails/referral-lead-notification.html in the Resend dashboard
# (see packages/ui/emails/README.md), then paste its ID into that file's
# `referralLeadNotification` key. Without an ID there the form still validates
# and shows success but does NOT send.

# Database (shared Neon Postgres).
# The referral form creates a client record in the unified `biz.clients` table
# (source: referral, carrying the referral code) via
# @jamie-nisbet/services; the email above is then just a notification. Without
# DATABASE_URL the form still works (email-only) and logs the lead. On Vercel this
# is provided by the Neon integration. Get the connection string from the Neon
# dashboard (pooled connection).
DATABASE_URL=
